Database Schema Documentation
Overview
•	Database System: DuckDB
•	Total Tables: 3
•	Total Records: 647,858
•	Analysis Period: 1900s–2020s
 
Data Volume Statistics
Table	Row Count	Primary Use
books	165,744	Core catalog and categorization
reviews	481,164	Popularity metrics and pricing
author_genders	50	Gender distribution analysis
 
Table: books
Description: Core book catalog with metadata, categorization, and temporal information
Row Count: 165,744
Column Name	Data Type	Nullable	Description
Title	VARCHAR	Yes	Full title of the book
authors	VARCHAR	Yes	JSON array of author names
publishedDate	VARCHAR	Yes	Publication date in various formats
categories	VARCHAR	Yes	JSON array of assigned categories
author_first_name	VARCHAR	Yes	Extracted first name of primary author
primary_category	VARCHAR	Yes	First/main category from categories array
Year	DOUBLE	Yes	Extracted publication year
Decade	DOUBLE	Yes	Calculated decade (floor(Year/10)*10)
Sample Data:
sql
Title: "Its Only Art If Its Well Hung!"
authors: ['Julie Strain']
publishedDate: "1996"
categories: ['Comics & Graphic Novels']
author_first_name: "Julie"
primary_category: "Comics & Graphic Novels"
Year: 1996.0
Decade: 1990.0
 
Table: reviews
Description: Customer reviews and pricing data
Row Count: 481,164
Column Name	Data Type	Nullable	Description
Title	VARCHAR	Yes	Book title (matches books table)
Price	DOUBLE	Yes	Book price in USD
review/score	DOUBLE	Yes	Customer rating (1.0–5.0 scale)
Sample Data:
Title: "Wonderful Worship in Smaller Churches"
Price: 19.4
review/score: 5.0
 


Table: author_genders
Description: Inferred gender data for authors based on first names
Row Count: 50
Column Name	Data Type	Nullable	Description
author_first_name	VARCHAR	Yes	Author's first name
book_count	BIGINT	Yes	Number of books by authors with this first name
inferred_gender	VARCHAR	Yes	Gender inference ("male"/"female")
gender_confidence	DOUBLE	Yes	Confidence score of gender inference (0.0–1.0)
Sample Data:
author_first_name: "John"
book_count: 4897
inferred_gender: "male"
gender_confidence: 1.0
 
Data Relationships
Primary Relationships
books.Title ───────┐
                   │
                   ├─→ reviews.Title (One-to-Many)
                   │
books.author_first_name ──→ author_genders.author_first_name (Many-to-One)

Join Patterns Used in Analysis
1.	Book-Review Join (for popularity scoring):
sql
FROM books b
LEFT JOIN reviews r ON b.Title = r.Title

2.	Book-Gender Join (for gender analysis):
sql
FROM books b
LEFT JOIN author_genders g ON b.author_first_name = g.author_first_name
 
